{"title":"Secant","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Secant</b> can refer to:\n</p>\n<ul><li>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Secant_line\" title=\"Secant line\">line</a> that passes through two points of a curve, like on a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">circle</a>.</li>\n<li>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Reciprocal\" title=\"Reciprocal\">reciprocal</a> of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cosine\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Cosine\">cosine</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trigonometry\" title=\"Trigonometry\">trigonometric</a> function.</li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Secant&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018110057\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.007 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.011 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 7/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 259/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.345      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.345      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4641:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018110057 and revision id 13317. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}